From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: The debugger of a crash shows no console.

A program that crashed opened a console window full of addresses
(winedbg --auto writing its backtrace), which Windows never shows: the
helpers of Discord's game capture did so at every screen share. The crash
is in the log already; the debugger gets a console nobody sees.
---
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
index c50ce42..e2f51ab 100644
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/debug.c
@@ -665,7 +665,12 @@ static BOOL start_debugger( EXCEPTION_POINTERS *epointers, HANDLE event )
     startup.cb = sizeof(startup);
     startup.dwFlags = STARTF_USESHOWWINDOW;
     startup.wShowWindow = SW_SHOWNORMAL;
-    ret = CreateProcessW( NULL, cmdline, NULL, NULL, TRUE, CREATE_UNICODE_ENVIRONMENT, env, NULL, &startup, &info );
+    /* Arctic: no console window full of addresses over the desktop, which
+     * Windows never shows: the crash is in the log already (report_crash),
+     * and the debugger, a console program, writes its own report to a
+     * console nobody sees */
+    ret = CreateProcessW( NULL, cmdline, NULL, NULL, TRUE, CREATE_UNICODE_ENVIRONMENT | CREATE_NO_WINDOW, env, NULL,
+                          &startup, &info );
     FreeEnvironmentStringsW( env );
 
     if (ret)
